{"id": "cf84a61c-cbed-4b7b-a7e0-97e18dfd329a", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm checking the IOPS-to-size ratio for io2 volumes: 20000 IOPS divided by 15 GiB gives 1333.3, which exceeds the documented maximum of 1000 IOPS per GiB for io2 (standard io2 allows 500 IOPS/GiB, Block Express allows 1000 IOPS/GiB), so that explains the error.

So 15 GiB caps at 15,000 IOPS max — the fix is either increasing the volume size to at least 20 GiB or lowering the requested IOPS to 15,000 or below, and I should mention ModifyVolume can change both together, plus the 6-hour cooldown between modifications.

"}]}
